{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1102797-assassin-s-creed","id":1102797,"title":"Assassin's Creed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-12T07:19:39-07:00","id":1102797,"title":"Assassin's Creed","content":"I'm about to finally pick up AC:Syndicate, and of course that got me thinking about Mage. A lot was made in the past about AC being very similar to Mage. I get the whole Templars=Technocracy, Assassins=Traditions thing, they are very similar. But in terms of what the factions DO, I just don't see it. What of what they do is magic, what isn't? A lot of the stuff I do in the games reminds me more of a Shadowrun physical adept, not an Ascension mage. But then again, I accept that I'm not very good at viewing Mage magic(k) as a more inward focused thing as opposed to a traditional mage view.<br /> <br /> So can anyone help enlighten me?<br /> <br /> While talking about Ubisoft games, one more thing. Does anyone else think WatchDogs is a great look at a Virtual Adept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T08:09:45-07:00","id":1102813,"title":"","content":"There's a long standing swashbuckling practice among Mages. There's a whole book about that for Crusade<br /> <br /> However, I would say that both Templars and Assassins are Technocracy/Order of Reason, or at least technomancers. At least in AC 2 you get to be friend with Leonardo da Vinci (a technomancer if there was ever one) and you get several somewhat unrealistic weapons like that hand dagger that has mechanisms to replegate in the wrist, but no way to grapple it, that could be easily treated as magical. The Animus it's magic, of course, Time 2. The assassination techniques that you use, and some of the parkour, could be magic improving your skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:06:39-07:00","id":1102848,"title":"","content":"I do think Watch Underscore Dogs is a great model for the Virtual Adepts. Hell, the game's hackers at their strongest can barely scratch the surface of what a VA could do with the right Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:48:28-07:00","id":1102867,"title":"","content":"The Templars &quot;taste&quot; like the Technocracy to me, and I could see a Traditionalist with magic like an Assassin (paging the Euthanatos), but I don't think it's a perfect fit. Honestly, the themes used for the Technocracy and the Templars are fairly normal for &quot;bad guys&quot; in Western media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T14:15:48-07:00","id":1102913,"title":"","content":"What's disturbing (or interesting, depending on your point of view) is that the real world history and assorted mythology built up around the two sects and their relationship with one another is far far weirder than any of the science fiction elements of the game. I'm honestly a little surprised that the history of Mage didn't involve the two sects fusing together into this weird collective of banker-assassins who became the foundation for the Syndicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T18:11:14-07:00","id":1103344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1102797-assassin-s-creed?p=1102813#post1102813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a long standing swashbuckling practice among Mages. There's a whole book about that for Crusade<br /> <br /> However, I would say that both Templars and Assassins are Technocracy/Order of Reason, or at least technomancers. At least in AC 2 you get to be friend with Leonardo da Vinci (a technomancer if there was ever one) and you get several somewhat unrealistic weapons like that hand dagger that has mechanisms to replegate in the wrist, but no way to grapple it, that could be easily treated as magical. The Animus it's magic, of course, Time 2. The assassination techniques that you use, and some of the parkour, could be magic improving your skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Leonardo strikes me as the sort of guy who'd work for whoever paid him because...well, he did.<br /> <br /> So I'd make him an Orphan Independent alchemist.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T07:24:20-07:00","id":1103476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">What's disturbing (or interesting, depending on your point of view) is that the real world history and assorted mythology built up around the two sects and their relationship with one another is far far weirder than any of the science fiction elements of the game. </span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's very interesting, especially the mytology. I think they still exist in the real world, with different names. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm honestly a little surprised that the history of Mage didn't involve the two sects fusing together into this weird collective of banker-assassins who became the foundation for the Syndicate.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Vampire owns the Assassins already (Assamites own Alamut, even if it's not the same Alamut, but a totally different Alamut that's near Alamut and controls or &quot;influences&quot; the assassin sect)<br /> <br /> But we do own the Templars...they were part of the OoR, and now are Disparate (and there's a few in the Chorus)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:55:38-07:00","id":1104027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1102797-assassin-s-creed?p=1103476#post1103476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's very interesting, especially the mytology. I think they still exist in the real world, with different names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nazari Shi'ites, of whom the Assassins were a part of, are still a large sect (second only in size to the Twelvers who are the official state religion of Iran) found around Asia, Africa and elsewhere. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire owns the Assassins already (Assamites own Alamut, even if it's not the same Alamut, but a totally different Alamut that's near Alamut and controls or &quot;influences&quot; the assassin sect) </div> </div> </div>Well, just because something is in Vampire doesn't necessarily mean it's true in Mage. Or that there aren't multiple supernatural conspiracies and subcultures trying to co-opt, influence, manipulate or otherwise horn in on any and every existing mundane mortal conspiracy or subcultures. I always felt one of the many missed opportunities of the long ago White Wolf Magazine was that there was never a (semi)regular bit on real world conspiracies, like the Assassins, and how you could incorporate them into the various game lines (Assamite front, Garou Kinfolk sect, proto-Ecstatics, pawns of a Mummy). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But we do own the Templars...they were part of the OoR, and now are Disparate (and there's a few in the Chorus) </div> </div> </div>When he was developer, Jess Heinig had wanted to do a Lost Paths: Knights Templar &amp; Lions of Zion book, with walking encyclopedia of conspiracies, occultism and weird history Ken Hite writing the Knights section and Richard Dansky writing the Lions. (Probably also talking about angels and their place in Mage.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:58:51-07:00","id":1104030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1102797-assassin-s-creed?p=1104027#post1104027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When he was developer, Jess Heinig had wanted to do a Lost Paths: Knights Templar &amp; Lions of Zion book, with walking encyclopedia of conspiracies, occultism and weird history Ken Hite writing the Knights section and Richard Dansky writing the Lions. (Probably also talking about angels and their place in Mage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, I wish that book had been made. It sounds so interesting. We could have had the Lions of Zion play more of a role than just as a footnote in Mage's canon.<br /> <br /> This truly is the most disappointing timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T17:23:33-07:00","id":1104043,"title":"","content":"There were several plans Jess had that sadly never came about for various reasons. Lost Paths was hoped to be a series (I think Wu Lung/Wu Keng and Children of Knowledge/Sisters of Hippolyta were the other two names tossed around, maybe Bata'a/N'goma too), as was Tales of Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T09:47:29-07:00","id":1104340,"title":"","content":"Actually, I would say that Assassins are pretty much Batini Magi, don't you think ? At least, they share some of the Credo. Batini are called the Subtle Ones and fight the Technocracy in the shadows since old Babylon ^^ What is Magick in AC is more a question of the philosophy than the techniques. Anyway, in the original plot (with the Eden fragments), one can say that there's something magickal about it. And they really do fight for Ascension, and like in Mage, Ascension and Armageddon are close things, which is the conclusion of the first AC trilogy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}